  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.4.1: two new compression levels, Statistical (TF-IDF word scoring) and Syntactic (rule-based grammatical-glue pruning with POS-gated hedge-clause elision), plus a new frequency-baseline Universal POS tagger (FunctionWordProvider.GetPosTags/GetPosTag) covering 54/55 languages, generated offline from the same Universal Dependencies data as lemmas/verbs. New retrieval/structure primitives: CavemanRetriever (BM25+ with optional RM3 pseudo-relevance-feedback query expansion), CavemanSimHash (near-duplicate text fingerprinting) powering CavemanLogCompressor.FuzzyFold, and CavemanTopicSegmenter (TextTiling topic segmentation) powering CavemanSummarizer.CondenseTextTopicAware. CavemanCodeCompressor gains an opt-in skeletonize parameter that collapses function bodies to signatures. Several correctness fixes found via a new comprehensibility test suite: cross-language generic-word contamination in Aggressive/Syntactic, a suffix heuristic that silently deleted Italian -are verbs and English financial/medical/legal-type adjectives, historical-treebank contamination in the Italian/Swedish/Romanian/Icelandic language data (an archaic sense of a word outvoting its modern meaning), and a tokenizer bug that fragmented words in scripts using combining marks (Kannada, Hindi, Tamil, Thai, ...). All changes are additive and backward-compatible.",
